Author:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Fri Dec 13 16:45:47 2024 +0000
Commit:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Fri Dec 13 16:45:47 2024 +0000

    Bug 1913580 - Part 5: Add getNativeTabProperties() and pass native tab properties into openTab(). r=mkmelin

    This patch introduces `getNativeTabProperties()`, similar to what we
    already do with `getNativeButtonProperties()`. The change in behavior
    here is not only that we add the new `userContextId` property, but also
    missing properties like `linkHandler`, `initialBrowsingContextGroupId`,
    and `triggeringPrincipal` (compare tabs created by the tabs API in [1]).

    This patch also includes a little bit of refactoring to reduce code
    duplication: the check for a valid URL is now handled in the new
    `getNativeTabProperties()` function.

    While working on this patch, I learned that the required preference
    `privacy.userContext.enabled` is automatically enabled, if the
    `contextualIdentities` permission is requested. The added test makes
    use of this permission. One of the older tests for the windows API is
    changed to test this mechanism there as well. The API description is
    updated accordingly.

    [1]: https://searchfox.org/comm-central/rev/ff577e4708535a1d59bc402ca2105e9592c254fb/mail/components/extensions/parent/ext-tabs.js#543-552

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D229975

